    "discussion": {
      "title": "Newton's Method",
      "subtitle": "Approximation Methods: Root-Finding",
      "text": "Newton's method finds a solution of $f(x) = 0$ by repeatedly creating tangent lines, replacing the current guess $x_n$ with the point where the tangent line at $x_n$ crosses the x-axis, $x_{n+1}$. For \"nice\" functions where $f'(x) \\neq 0$, Newton's method will find a root of $f(x)$."
    }
